1
00:01:06,392 --> 00:01:08,723
<i>For those who have not read the plaque,</i>

2
00:01:08,747 --> 00:01:10,638
<i>we will read the plaque.</i>

3
00:01:11,638 --> 00:01:13,610
<i>Here men from the planet Earth</i>

4
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,685
<i>first set foot upon the moon</i>

5
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:18,494
<i>July 1969.</i>

6
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:22,397
<i>We came in peace for all mankind.</i>

7
00:03:02,668 --> 00:03:05,799
If this isn't an insanely beautiful woman,
I am hanging up.

8
00:03:05,878 --> 00:03:06,504
<i>Sir.</i>

9
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:08,473
I-I-I think you should listen to this.

10
00:03:17,183 --> 00:03:18,603
Sir?
<i>Goddamn it!</i>

11
00:03:18,968 --> 00:03:19,464
<i>Damn!</i>

12
00:03:19,489 --> 00:03:20,489
Sir?
<i>Damn.</i>

13
00:03:21,327 --> 00:03:24,126
Come on baby. Come on baby.
Come on baby. Come on.

14
00:03:24,312 --> 00:03:26,678
This better not be another
damn Russian spy job!

15
00:03:26,703 --> 00:03:29,078
Boys from Air Traffic Res say
the skies are clear.

16
00:03:29,412 --> 00:03:30,530
It's the real thing.

17
00:03:31,096 --> 00:03:32,867
A radio signal from another world.

18
00:03:33,325 --> 00:03:35,375
Let-Let's-Let's not jump the gun here.

19
00:03:35,457 --> 00:03:37,996
Get online with Space Command.
They are gonna want to know about...

20
00:03:38,705 --> 00:03:41,184
what's with the golf balls.
You are gonna kill me here.

21
00:03:41,398 --> 00:03:42,804
Wait. Wait. This can't be right.

22
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:45,556
The calculated distance from source...

23
00:03:45,704 --> 00:03:48,904
is only 375,000km.

24
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,554
It's coming from the moon.

25
00:04:07,024 --> 00:04:08,457
Who else knows about this?

26
00:04:08,598 --> 00:04:11,262
S.E.T.I. in New Mexico identified a signal.

27
00:04:11,287 --> 00:04:12,187
But...

28
00:04:12,798 --> 00:04:14,989
they are even more confused
than we are sir.

29
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,681
Excuse me.

30
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,535
Major!
Yes sir.

31
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:25,149
Radar reception has been impaired

32
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:26,900
but we were able to get these.

33
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:32,477
We estimate that it has a diameter
of over 550km,

34
00:04:32,517 --> 00:04:35,368
and a mass roughly one
fourth the size of our moon.

35
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,300
What the hell is it?

36
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:39,502
A meteor?
No sir.

37
00:04:39,636 --> 00:04:40,837
No, definitely not.

38
00:04:41,438 --> 00:04:42,508
How do you know?

39
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,313
Well sir, it's slowing down.

40
00:04:45,016 --> 00:04:46,121
It's what?

41
00:04:46,434 --> 00:04:47,313
It's...

42
00:04:47,466 --> 00:04:48,773
It's slowing down sir.

43
00:04:57,117 --> 00:04:58,958
Get me the Secretary of Defense.

44
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:01,232
Then wake him!

45
00:05:05,511 --> 00:05:06,385
Hello.

46
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:07,635
<i>Hi.</i> It's me.

47
00:05:08,324 --> 00:05:09,126
<i>Hi.</i>

48
00:05:10,251 --> 00:05:11,471
<i>What time is it there?</i>

49
00:05:11,882 --> 00:05:13,624
It's 2:45 in the morning.

50
00:05:13,873 --> 00:05:15,224
<i>I know I didn't wake you.</i>

51
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,056
As a matter of fact, you did.

52
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,398
Liar.

53
00:05:20,703 --> 00:05:22,336
I have a confession to make.

54
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,770
I am sleeping...

55
00:05:23,794 --> 00:05:26,250
next to a beautiful young brunette.

56
00:05:27,795 --> 00:05:29,662
<i>You didn't let her stay up
all night watching TV?</i>

57
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:30,944
Did you?

58
00:05:30,968 --> 00:05:31,975
<i>Of course not.</i>

59
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:34,206
You are gonna come home right
after the luncheon right?

60
00:05:34,231 --> 00:05:35,431
<i>Yes, yes, yes, yes.</i>

61
00:05:35,456 --> 00:05:36,335
Mommy?

62
00:05:36,811 --> 00:05:37,858
Here is your mother.

63
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:41,859
<i>Hi honey!</i>

64
00:05:42,424 --> 00:05:43,617
Hi. I miss you.

65
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:46,312
<i>I know, I miss you too.
President Whitmore's approval ratings</i>

66
00:05:46,383 --> 00:05:48,413
<i>have slipped below 40%.</i>

67
00:05:48,562 --> 00:05:50,659
<i>Even his crime bill failed to pass.</i>
He is good.

68
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:53,591
<i>Are the salad days over for
President Whitmore?</i>

69
00:05:53,615 --> 00:05:54,514
<i>More talk.</i>

70
00:05:54,619 --> 00:05:56,779
<i>Leadership as a pilot in the Gulf War</i>

71
00:05:56,804 --> 00:05:59,506
<i>is completely different from
leadership in politics.</i>

72
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,254
Daddy let me watch Letterman.

73
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:03,137
Traitor.

74
00:06:03,178 --> 00:06:06,168
<i>That's the problem.
They elected a warrior and they got a wimp.</i>

75
00:06:06,594 --> 00:06:07,855
Good morning George.

76
00:06:07,964 --> 00:06:09,176
Good morning Mr. President.

77
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,700
That game could not have been pretty.

78
00:06:12,248 --> 00:06:13,298
Thank you sir.

79
00:06:14,721 --> 00:06:17,121
Connie you are up awfully early this morning.

80
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:21,509
They are not attacking your policies sir.

81
00:06:21,571 --> 00:06:22,995
They are attacking your age.

82
00:06:23,084 --> 00:06:25,099
Whitmore seems less like the president

83
00:06:25,124 --> 00:06:28,261
and more like the orphan child Oliver asking.

84
00:06:28,285 --> 00:06:29,932
Please sir I would like some more.

85
00:06:31,159 --> 00:06:32,038
That's clever.

86
00:06:32,171 --> 00:06:33,933
Yeah well I am not laughing.

87
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:36,600
Age was never an issue
when you stuck to your guns.

88
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,925
You were thought of as young idealistic.
Thanks.

89
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:39,750
Now...

90
00:06:40,075 --> 00:06:41,702
the message has gotten lost.

91
00:06:42,078 --> 00:06:43,660
It's just too much politics

92
00:06:43,685 --> 00:06:45,004
too much compromise.

93
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:49,300
Isn't it amazing how quickly
everyone can turn against you?

94
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,300
It's a fine line between standing behind
a principle and...

95
00:06:56,498 --> 00:06:57,623
hiding behind one.

96
00:06:58,450 --> 00:06:59,950
You can tolerate a little compromise

97
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,350
if you are actually managing
to get something accomplished.

98
00:07:03,818 --> 00:07:04,562
Well...

99
00:07:05,326 --> 00:07:09,751
The Orange County Dispatch has voted you
one of the ten sexiest men...

100
00:07:10,228 --> 00:07:11,318
of the year.

101
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:14,000
That's...

102
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:18,140
That's accomplishing something.

103
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:20,078
Excuse me Mr. President.

104
00:07:20,603 --> 00:07:22,074
It's the Secretary of Defense.

105
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:25,974
Yes.

106
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:31,270
Could you say that again?

107
00:08:02,045 --> 00:08:04,367
<i>Station WXBY out here in Brooklyn.</i>

108
00:08:04,494 --> 00:08:07,412
<i>The temperature is 95
degrees in Central Park.</i>

109
00:08:07,552 --> 00:08:09,542
<i>What it is here in the borough
God only knows.</i>

110
00:08:09,731 --> 00:08:10,832
<i>Let's go to Nick Jones.</i>

111
00:08:10,864 --> 00:08:12,668
<i>He will give us a traffic
report to the beaches...</i>

112
00:08:14,728 --> 00:08:15,824
So what are you waiting?

113
00:08:17,012 --> 00:08:19,312
My Social Security will expire
you will still be sitting there.

114
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,102
I am thinking.

115
00:08:21,696 --> 00:08:23,188
Yeah well think already!

116
00:08:31,327 --> 00:08:34,045
Have you any idea how long it takes
for those things to decompose?

117
00:08:34,545 --> 00:08:36,623
If you don't move soon
I am gonna start to decompose.

118
00:08:42,896 --> 00:08:44,684
Listen David, I have been meaning
to talk with you.

119
00:08:47,076 --> 00:08:49,380
It's nice that you see me so much now but...
Don't.

120
00:08:49,405 --> 00:08:50,663
Don't start Dad.

121
00:08:50,688 --> 00:08:53,122
I am only saying it's been what?
Four years?

122
00:08:53,147 --> 00:08:54,495
You are still wearing a wedding band?

123
00:08:55,029 --> 00:08:55,692
Three years.

124
00:08:55,717 --> 00:08:58,271
Alright three, four. You are divorced.
Come on. Move on.

125
00:08:58,333 --> 00:08:59,178
This is not healthy.

126
00:08:59,203 --> 00:09:01,958
No this is not healthy.
Smoking is not healthy.

127
00:09:06,933 --> 00:09:07,776
Checkmate.

128
00:09:08,916 --> 00:09:10,533
Wait a minute, wait a minute,
wait a minute.

129
00:09:11,104 --> 00:09:12,544
Wait, wait, wait. This is not...

130
00:09:12,673 --> 00:09:13,754
This is not checkmate.

131
00:09:13,935 --> 00:09:14,735
See you tomorrow Pop.

132
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:16,512
No, no, no, just hold on.
This is not checkmate.

133
00:09:20,498 --> 00:09:21,498
Checkmate.

134
00:09:21,703 --> 00:09:23,882
Yes, we have got everybody we have
working on the problem.

135
00:09:24,978 --> 00:09:27,429
I love XFiles too.
I hope you get to see it.

136
00:09:29,992 --> 00:09:31,452
David! David!

137
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,062
What's the hell is the point of having a beeper
if you are not gonna turn it on?

138
00:09:34,087 --> 00:09:35,701
It was turned on, I was ignoring you.

139
00:09:35,726 --> 00:09:36,998
Hello. What's the...

140
00:09:37,216 --> 00:09:38,304
What's the big emergency?

141
00:09:38,528 --> 00:09:39,927
It started this morning.

142
00:09:39,965 --> 00:09:42,188
Every station's making like it's the 1950s.

143
00:09:42,558 --> 00:09:45,394
We got static. We got snow.
All kinds of distortions.

144
00:09:45,541 --> 00:09:46,680
Nobody knows...

145
00:09:47,023 --> 00:09:49,789
What are you doing? There is a reason
we have bins labeled recycle.

146
00:09:49,996 --> 00:09:51,306
What the hell is going on?

147
00:09:51,469 --> 00:09:52,651
My God in heaven.

148
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:54,540
So sue me. David!

149
00:09:54,688 --> 00:09:55,934
We got a problem.

150
00:09:56,110 --> 00:09:58,225
Did you try to switch transponder channels?

151
00:09:58,317 --> 00:10:01,379
Oh please. You think I would be this
panicked if it was something simple?

152
00:10:01,469 --> 00:10:02,243
Ok. Let's...

153
00:10:02,447 --> 00:10:04,146
point the dish at another satellite.

154
00:10:04,311 --> 00:10:06,295
We tried that. It didn't work.

155
00:10:06,674 --> 00:10:08,938
It's almost as though
they were not even there.

156
00:10:09,291 --> 00:10:10,974
Alright. What have we got here?

157
00:10:16,959 --> 00:10:18,051
This is impossible.

158
00:10:18,431 --> 00:10:20,325
<i>We created a race of robots.</i>

159
00:10:20,544 --> 00:10:21,726
<i>Their function...</i>

160
00:10:22,471 --> 00:10:24,176
Miguel the signal is all screwed up.

161
00:10:24,442 --> 00:10:25,279
Stop it.

162
00:10:25,303 --> 00:10:26,423
Just leave it alone.

163
00:10:26,482 --> 00:10:27,716
You are gonna break it alright?

164
00:10:27,826 --> 00:10:29,101
It's so fuzzy.

165
00:10:37,183 --> 00:10:38,428
Oh no.

166
00:10:43,121 --> 00:10:44,269
Good morning Lucas.

167
00:10:45,076 --> 00:10:46,325
You see these?

168
00:10:46,935 --> 00:10:49,387
I got a whole god damn crop,
full of these.

169
00:10:49,759 --> 00:10:51,708
If your father is not in the air
in 20 minutes...

170
00:10:52,977 --> 00:10:54,393
I am getting someone else.

171
00:11:03,427 --> 00:11:04,575
Hey Russell!

172
00:11:04,812 --> 00:11:06,224
Hey Miguel!

173
00:11:19,769 --> 00:11:21,430
Russell!
What are you doing?

174
00:11:37,806 --> 00:11:39,464
Just what in the hell
do you think you are doing?

175
00:11:43,726 --> 00:11:45,565
It's the wrong field you idiot.

176
00:11:45,966 --> 00:11:48,290
Lucas' farm is on the other side of town.

177
00:11:51,692 --> 00:11:52,939
Are you sure?

178
00:12:32,581 --> 00:12:34,431
CNS is running a story
that we are covering up

179
00:12:34,456 --> 00:12:36,235
some type of nuclear testing experiment.

180
00:12:36,259 --> 00:12:38,666
So tell them to run with it if they
want to embarrass themselves.

181
00:12:38,769 --> 00:12:40,260
NASA's been on my butt all morning.

182
00:12:40,284 --> 00:12:41,323
They want to know our position.

183
00:12:41,348 --> 00:12:45,283
Our official position is
we have no official position.

184
00:12:45,308 --> 00:12:47,364
Connie what is going on here?

185
00:12:47,365 --> 00:12:49,840
Come on guys,
would I keep you out of the loop?

186
00:12:49,865 --> 00:12:51,099
Yes absolutely.
In a second.

187
00:12:51,195 --> 00:12:52,950
So what?
I can't hear you.

188
00:12:53,316 --> 00:12:55,818
At the moment our satellites are
somewhat unreliable.

189
00:12:55,843 --> 00:12:59,120
Isn't it possible that this thing
may just pass us by?

190
00:12:59,145 --> 00:13:01,065
What if it doesn't pass us by?

191
00:13:01,233 --> 00:13:03,823
Let's re-target some ICBMs
to blow it out of the sky.

192
00:13:03,848 --> 00:13:06,573
And risk turning one dangerous
falling object into many?

193
00:13:06,818 --> 00:13:08,942
We don't yet know enough
about what we are dealing with

194
00:13:08,967 --> 00:13:10,781
to make any kind of intelligent judgments.

195
00:13:10,949 --> 00:13:13,703
Luckily the press is making up
their own story at this point.

196
00:13:14,316 --> 00:13:15,630
But that's not gonna keep.

197
00:13:16,352 --> 00:13:18,530
We may need to upgrade to DEFCON 3.

198
00:13:18,531 --> 00:13:19,547
Absolutely.

199
00:13:19,572 --> 00:13:20,692
General contact NORAD.

200
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:22,495
You tell them we have upgraded
to DEFCON 3.

201
00:13:22,519 --> 00:13:23,758
That's not what the President said.

202
00:13:24,073 --> 00:13:25,626
Don't you think that's a little premature?
I don't think so.

203
00:13:25,651 --> 00:13:29,020
We have over 50% of the armed forces
out on weekend leave.

204
00:13:29,045 --> 00:13:32,904
Not to mention, the commanders and troops
that are in town for the 4th of July parade.

205
00:13:33,044 --> 00:13:34,150
Go ahead Commander.
Our intelligence,

206
00:13:34,174 --> 00:13:36,471
tells us the object
has settled into a stationary orbit.

207
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:37,869
Well, that's good news.

208
00:13:38,473 --> 00:13:39,504
Not really sir.

209
00:13:39,982 --> 00:13:42,684
Part of it has broken off into nearly
three dozen other pieces

210
00:13:43,016 --> 00:13:44,727
smaller than the whole sir

211
00:13:45,348 --> 00:13:47,520
yet over 15 miles in width themselves.

212
00:13:51,465 --> 00:13:52,736
Where are they heading?

213
00:13:53,205 --> 00:13:56,083
They should be entering our atmosphere
within the next 25 minutes.

214
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,985
Take us to DEFCON 3.

215
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:17,688
Please tell me we are getting somewhere.

216
00:14:17,813 --> 00:14:19,524
Oh there is good news
and there is bad news.

217
00:14:19,550 --> 00:14:21,200
Alright. What's the bad news?

218
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,999
The bad news is there is no
penalty for disturbing my lunch.

219
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,100
And the good news is
you are not gonna charge me.

220
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:27,663
No the good news,

221
00:14:27,688 --> 00:14:29,566
is that I found the problem.
It's not our equipment.

222
00:14:29,591 --> 00:14:31,684
It's some kind of weird signal
embedded in the satellite feed.

223
00:14:32,317 --> 00:14:33,617
Wait that's the good news?

224
00:14:34,050 --> 00:14:36,100
Yeah, because this signal
has a definite sequential pattern.

225
00:14:36,254 --> 00:14:38,054
So as soon as I find
the exact binary sequence

226
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:41,730
then I can calculate the phase reversal with that
analyzer I bought for your birthday and apply it

227
00:14:42,344 --> 00:14:43,761
we should be able to block it out completely.

228
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:48,000
And then we will be the only guys in town
with a clear picture!

229
00:14:48,199 --> 00:14:50,460
Yes! Yes! Yes! Oh David!

230
00:14:50,485 --> 00:14:51,760
That's why I love you!

231
00:14:52,204 --> 00:14:53,254
That's not necessary.
Yes!

232
00:14:53,698 --> 00:14:54,748
Yes!
Too kind.

233
00:15:23,674 --> 00:15:25,497
This better be good.
Captain on deck!

234
00:15:29,203 --> 00:15:32,892
Sir we are looking at a total radar
blackout over a 13 km area.

235
00:15:33,063 --> 00:15:35,573
Let's do a diagnostic check...
Excuse me sir.

236
00:15:36,166 --> 00:15:38,685
The radar may be malfunctioning
but the infrared

237
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:40,134
is totally off the map.

238
00:15:44,656 --> 00:15:45,699
Jeez.

239
00:15:48,790 --> 00:15:50,671
Get me Atlantic Command on the line.

240
00:15:53,738 --> 00:15:54,738
Hang on sir.

241
00:15:54,762 --> 00:15:58,102
Sir, we have visual range
with incoming over Iraqi airspace.

242
00:15:58,227 --> 00:15:59,345
Second sighting?

243
00:15:59,369 --> 00:16:01,502
Yes sir.
This just came in from the Persian Gulf.

244
00:16:03,026 --> 00:16:04,026
Correction sir.

245
00:16:04,033 --> 00:16:06,008
<i>We now have two confirmed
visual contacts.</i>

246
00:16:06,032 --> 00:16:07,384
That's affirmative. Mr. President.

247
00:16:07,409 --> 00:16:10,184
They are tracking another one
off the California coastline.

248
00:16:10,877 --> 00:16:12,072
Alright go ahead.
Put it on.

249
00:16:12,097 --> 00:16:13,985
General you might want to watch this.
Yes sir.

250
00:16:17,271 --> 00:16:18,480
<i>Ladies and gentlemen.</i>

251
00:16:18,779 --> 00:16:19,771
<i>Ladies and gentlemen</i>

252
00:16:19,796 --> 00:16:21,528
<i>we are interrupting our regular broadcast</i>

253
00:16:21,661 --> 00:16:22,936
<i>to bring you extraordinary events</i>

254
00:16:22,961 --> 00:16:24,619
<i>taking place in the Russian Republic.</i>

255
00:16:24,643 --> 00:16:26,153
<i>This unexplained disturbance</i>

256
00:16:26,177 --> 00:16:29,405
<i>and the hysteria that it's
causing are incredible.</i>

257
00:16:29,609 --> 00:16:32,194
<i>How would you describe
what you are seeing?</i>

258
00:16:32,382 --> 00:16:33,874
<i>It is clearing the mountains</i>

259
00:16:34,288 --> 00:16:38,006
<i>moving too slowly to be a comet
or meteor.</i>

260
00:16:38,411 --> 00:16:41,371
<i>Widespread panic has gripped
the countryside</i>

261
00:16:41,396 --> 00:16:44,371
<i>as thousands have taken to the streets.</i>

262
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,910
<i>It is confirmed.</i>

263
00:16:46,332 --> 00:16:49,184
<i>The unexplained phenomenon
is headed for Moscow.</i>

264
00:16:49,414 --> 00:16:51,989
Mr. President we have
an AWAC off the West Coast.

265
00:16:52,044 --> 00:16:54,161
ETA with contact point three minutes.

266
00:16:55,917 --> 00:16:58,442
I don't understand it sir.
Side radar doesn't see it.

267
00:16:59,092 --> 00:17:00,491
I know. It's blind sir.

268
00:17:00,529 --> 00:17:01,904
Nothing is registering.

269
00:17:01,945 --> 00:17:04,120
Negative.
We have zero visibility.

270
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:06,214
Visibility is at zero.

271
00:17:06,215 --> 00:17:08,256
Command this is Eagle Eye 370.

272
00:17:09,156 --> 00:17:11,098
Captain the president is listening.

273
00:17:11,157 --> 00:17:13,006
Repeat what you just told me.

274
00:17:14,545 --> 00:17:16,871
<i>We still have zero visibility.</i>

275
00:17:18,902 --> 00:17:20,816
<i>Instrumentation is malfunctioning.</i>

276
00:17:22,044 --> 00:17:24,767
<i>We can't get any kind of reading
of what's in front of us.</i>

277
00:17:25,354 --> 00:17:26,388
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

278
00:17:27,941 --> 00:17:28,922
<i>Maybe clearing.</i>

279
00:17:37,288 --> 00:17:38,829
Pull up! Pull up!

280
00:17:49,873 --> 00:17:51,081
Line is gone sir.

281
00:17:51,234 --> 00:17:52,908
Two more have been spotted
over the Atlantic.

282
00:17:53,033 --> 00:17:54,299
One is moving toward New York

283
00:17:54,402 --> 00:17:55,533
the other's headed this direction.

284
00:17:55,588 --> 00:17:57,594
How much time do we have?
Less than 10 minutes.

285
00:17:57,619 --> 00:17:59,094
Alex organize a military escort.

286
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,828
Mr. President I strongly recommend

287
00:18:00,853 --> 00:18:03,104
we move you to a secure
location immediately.

288
00:18:03,105 --> 00:18:05,763
Connie can we expect the same
kind of panic we saw in Russia?

289
00:18:05,788 --> 00:18:06,962
More than likely.
Mister President.

290
00:18:06,987 --> 00:18:08,362
We can discuss this on the way.

291
00:18:08,942 --> 00:18:10,183
I am not leaving.

292
00:18:11,296 --> 00:18:13,467
We have to maintain
a working government...

293
00:18:13,492 --> 00:18:14,901
I want you to get the vice president

294
00:18:14,925 --> 00:18:16,466
the whole cabinet and joint chiefs

295
00:18:16,525 --> 00:18:18,482
and take them to a secured location.

296
00:18:18,507 --> 00:18:19,423
I am staying.

297
00:18:19,813 --> 00:18:23,221
I don't want to add to a public hysteria
that's gonna cost lives.

298
00:18:23,981 --> 00:18:25,223
Connie.
Yes sir.

299
00:18:25,247 --> 00:18:27,647
We will initiate the Emergency
Broadcast System.

300
00:18:27,714 --> 00:18:29,678
We will advise people, not to panic.

301
00:18:29,929 --> 00:18:31,307
The best idea right now,

302
00:18:31,804 --> 00:18:32,885
is to stay in their homes.

303
00:18:33,022 --> 00:18:33,851
Yes sir.

304
00:18:33,875 --> 00:18:34,819
Roy. Dean.

305
00:18:34,844 --> 00:18:36,837
Alex you contact the cabinet members.

306
00:18:36,978 --> 00:18:38,103
Have them rendezvous here.

307
00:18:38,128 --> 00:18:39,245
We will take them to NORAD.

308
00:18:40,326 --> 00:18:43,159
Mr. President with your permission
I would like to remain at your side.

309
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:47,308
I had a feeling you would.

310
00:18:50,013 --> 00:18:52,719
And what happens if they do become hostile?

311
00:18:54,906 --> 00:18:56,274
Then God help us.

312
00:18:57,132 --> 00:18:59,530
<i>There it is the strange
atmospheric phenomenon.</i>

313
00:18:59,585 --> 00:19:03,132
<i>It is apparently what has been causing
all the distortions in our broadcasts.</i>

314
00:19:03,178 --> 00:19:04,677
David are you watching this?

315
00:19:07,226 --> 00:19:09,858
<i>Not to react in a manner of cold fear.</i>

316
00:19:10,443 --> 00:19:14,257
<i>We have no evidence that these
phenomena are endangering anyone.</i>

317
00:19:15,014 --> 00:19:16,879
<i>Thus far reports of aggression</i>

318
00:19:17,232 --> 00:19:18,896
Well, Marty li-li-listen to this.

319
00:19:18,921 --> 00:19:22,003
I got a lock on the pattern of that
signal so we can filter it out but...

320
00:19:22,304 --> 00:19:25,175
if my calculations are right it's going
to be gone in like seven hours anyway.

321
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,468
It's reducing itself every time it recycles

322
00:19:27,918 --> 00:19:30,421
so eventually it's gonna disappear...

323
00:19:31,075 --> 00:19:33,300
You listening?
Can you believe this.

324
00:19:36,082 --> 00:19:37,615
David have not you been watching?

325
00:19:38,189 --> 00:19:39,256
David!
<i>General.</i>

326
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,379
<i>General.</i>

327
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,022
<i>Good afternoon.</i>

328
00:19:42,570 --> 00:19:45,145
<i>So far the phenomenon has
not caused any damage.</i>

329
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,394
We have to ask you to try to stay calm

330
00:19:47,418 --> 00:19:49,586
and it's important for everyone not to panic.

331
00:19:50,145 --> 00:19:52,864
<i>We have a fix on three
of the occurrences about to appear...</i>

332
00:19:53,044 --> 00:19:54,644
<i>over American cities.</i>
It's just unreal.

333
00:19:55,351 --> 00:19:56,387
Hey Miguel come here.

334
00:19:56,412 --> 00:19:58,285
<i>One is headed towards Los Angeles.</i>

335
00:19:58,349 --> 00:20:00,341
<i>The other two are on our eastern seaboard</i>

336
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:01,522
<i>headed towards New York,</i>

337
00:20:01,999 --> 00:20:03,381
<i>and Washington D.C.</i>

338
00:20:04,315 --> 00:20:05,315
Marty. Marty.

339
00:20:05,339 --> 00:20:08,201
Jamie says this building
has an old bomb shelter.

340
00:20:08,613 --> 00:20:09,852
We are heading down there now.

341
00:20:10,113 --> 00:20:13,169
Alright, alright everybody,
head down to the basement.

342
00:20:13,270 --> 00:20:14,811
Take it slow.
Don't run.

343
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,486
Walk down to the basement.

344
00:20:18,444 --> 00:20:20,317
There is no shame in hiding.

345
00:20:21,143 --> 00:20:22,880
Oh I better call my mother.

346
00:20:34,398 --> 00:20:37,247
Well look who we have here.

347
00:20:40,963 --> 00:20:43,811
Hey Russ I heard you had a little trouble
this morning.

348
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:45,438
Dusted the wrong field.

349
00:20:46,862 --> 00:20:49,786
Well I know you are probably still
a little confused

350
00:20:49,811 --> 00:20:51,494
from your hostage experience.

351
00:20:51,594 --> 00:20:53,068
Hostage experience.

352
00:20:53,476 --> 00:20:55,076
Did something happen to you Russ?

353
00:20:55,151 --> 00:20:56,201
Oh yeah.

354
00:20:56,225 --> 00:20:58,334
Seems years back our boy
was kidnapped by aliens.

355
00:20:58,359 --> 00:20:59,303
Did all kind...

356
