01:01:57,605 --> 01:01:59,174
<i>Damn. They got shields too.</i>

1023
01:02:10,774 --> 01:02:12,711
<i>Let's go Knights.
Move Knights move!</i>

1024
01:02:17,731 --> 01:02:18,688
<i>Jesus.</i>

1025
01:02:19,318 --> 01:02:21,325
They got another one sir.
Two more just went down.

1026
01:02:21,500 --> 01:02:23,224
They are dropping like flies.
We are losing them.

1027
01:02:23,482 --> 01:02:24,828
Alright. Get them out of there.

1028
01:02:25,583 --> 01:02:27,677
Alright. Squadron leaders
retreat to fallback positions.

1029
01:02:27,702 --> 01:02:29,878
Abort mission. Abort mission right away.
Do you read me?

1030
01:02:29,903 --> 01:02:30,880
Do you copy?

1031
01:02:34,466 --> 01:02:36,372
<i>Alright, I think we are going to make
a run for this one here.</i>

1032
01:02:36,397 --> 01:02:37,606
<i>Let's get low.
Let's get fast.</i>

1033
01:02:37,938 --> 01:02:39,748
<i>I got you big daddy.
Let's get them.</i>

1034
01:02:42,356 --> 01:02:43,373
<i>Watch the deck.</i>

1035
01:02:51,358 --> 01:02:52,548
Do you read me your postion?

1036
01:02:52,572 --> 01:02:53,819
Squadron Leader do you read?

1037
01:02:53,844 --> 01:02:55,578
This isn't happening fast enough.
Abort!

1038
01:02:55,617 --> 01:02:56,836
Get them out of there!

1039
01:03:03,300 --> 01:03:05,612
What's with the monitor?
Where is the picture?

1040
01:03:05,937 --> 01:03:07,080
We have lost the satellite.

1041
01:03:11,754 --> 01:03:13,528
<i>We got two R-6 Jimmy. Check them.</i>

1042
01:03:13,700 --> 01:03:14,396
<i>Roger.</i>

1043
01:03:16,204 --> 01:03:18,310
<i>Come on, come on, come on, come on.
Move, move, move!</i>

1044
01:03:19,217 --> 01:03:21,396
<i>He is on me like white on rice big daddy.</i>

1045
01:03:21,421 --> 01:03:22,578
<i>Alright Jimmy.
They ain't got nothing for us.</i>

1046
01:03:22,603 --> 01:03:24,014
<i>Let's push it.
We got to go! We got to go!</i>

1047
01:03:24,215 --> 01:03:25,976
<i>I can't shake them. I can't shake them.</i>

1048
01:03:26,001 --> 01:03:27,972
<i>Yes you can. Just the way
I showed you. Let's go!</i>

1049
01:03:28,032 --> 01:03:29,863
<i>Check me out.
Maybe I am going to try something.</i>

1050
01:03:29,888 --> 01:03:31,277
<i>Don't do nothing stupid over there.</i>

1051
01:03:31,302 --> 01:03:33,299
<i>You know me.
That's what I am talking about.</i>

1052
01:03:33,876 --> 01:03:36,163
<i>Jimmy! Jimmy! What are you doing?
You can't bank at that speed.</i>

1053
01:03:37,102 --> 01:03:38,483
<i>Jimmy he is closing on you!</i>

1054
01:03:41,640 --> 01:03:43,015
<i>Put your mask back on!</i>

1055
01:03:43,039 --> 01:03:44,244
<i>That's an order Marine!</i>

1056
01:03:44,269 --> 01:03:45,379
<i>I can't breathe!</i>

1057
01:03:46,163 --> 01:03:47,116
<i>Jimmy!</i>

1058
01:03:48,684 --> 01:03:49,894
<i>Jimmy!</i>

1059
01:03:52,216 --> 01:03:54,167
<i>Jimmy! No!</i>

1060
01:03:54,658 --> 01:03:56,190
That's affirmative.
We have incoming.

1061
01:03:56,215 --> 01:03:57,653
Let me have it son.
You got it.

1062
01:03:58,911 --> 01:03:59,682
Friendly?

1063
01:04:01,109 --> 01:04:02,009
Sergeant?

1064
01:04:02,563 --> 01:04:03,682
I don't think so.

1065
01:04:08,942 --> 01:04:10,570
Go! Go! Go! Go!

1066
01:04:31,765 --> 01:04:33,484
<i>Come on and get me!
Come and get me!</i>

1067
01:04:37,942 --> 01:04:39,280
<i>What are you shooting at?</i>

1068
01:04:40,658 --> 01:04:43,062
<i>Where you at baby?
Come on! Come on!</i>

1069
01:04:48,648 --> 01:04:49,858
<i>You can't hit nothing!</i>

1070
01:05:08,324 --> 01:05:09,258
<i>Low bridge!</i>

1071
01:05:13,712 --> 01:05:15,348
<i>See if you can fly that thing undercover.</i>

1072
01:05:20,361 --> 01:05:21,938
<i>Hope you got an air bag.</i>

1073
01:05:59,338 --> 01:06:00,358
Son of a bitch.

1074
01:06:05,133 --> 01:06:07,022
That's right!
That's right!

1075
01:06:07,356 --> 01:06:08,908
Get off of me!
Get off of me!

1076
01:06:09,188 --> 01:06:10,444
That's what you get!

1077
01:06:11,742 --> 01:06:12,542
Look at you!

1078
01:06:12,619 --> 01:06:14,163
Ship all banged up!

1079
01:06:14,331 --> 01:06:15,574
Who is the man?

1080
01:06:16,363 --> 01:06:17,475
Who is the man?

1081
01:06:17,606 --> 01:06:19,051
Wait until I get another plane!

1082
01:06:19,126 --> 01:06:21,571
I am lining all your friends up,
right beside you!

1083
01:06:22,941 --> 01:06:23,946
Where you at?

1084
01:06:24,547 --> 01:06:25,575
Where you at?

1085
01:06:37,604 --> 01:06:38,708
Welcome to Earth.

1086
01:06:50,044 --> 01:06:51,912
Now that's what I call a close encounter.

1087
01:06:57,457 --> 01:06:59,502
Baby stay right here.
Stay right here with Boomer.

1088
01:07:09,132 --> 01:07:10,159
Keys.

1089
01:07:10,385 --> 01:07:11,760
Come on. Keys.

1090
01:07:12,346 --> 01:07:13,181
Yes!

1091
01:07:13,848 --> 01:07:15,402
Come on baby.
Come on.

1092
01:07:15,772 --> 01:07:16,819
Come on.

1093
01:07:17,869 --> 01:07:18,619
Yes.

1094
01:07:18,644 --> 01:07:22,557
<i>Rumor reports indicate that this battle
has repeated itself all over the world</i>

1095
01:07:22,582 --> 01:07:24,126
<i>with the exact same results.</i>

1096
01:07:25,100 --> 01:07:26,679
You are just like your mother you know that?

1097
01:07:27,559 --> 01:07:28,888
She was stubborn too.

1098
01:07:29,557 --> 01:07:32,143
I had to twist her arm
to get her to take her medicine.

1099
01:07:33,800 --> 01:07:35,026
You are gonna be alright.

1100
01:07:36,145 --> 01:07:37,299
You are gonna be fine.

1101
01:07:40,004 --> 01:07:42,218
You see Troy?
You are feeling better already.

1102
01:07:44,300 --> 01:07:45,617
I could not find anything.

1103
01:07:45,771 --> 01:07:47,524
Everyone is packing up.
They are leaving.

1104
01:07:47,800 --> 01:07:49,803
They said there is a spaceship
heading this way.

1105
01:07:49,859 --> 01:07:51,159
We would better leave too then.

1106
01:07:53,870 --> 01:07:56,120
Penicillin. At least it will help you
keep his fever down.

1107
01:07:56,700 --> 01:07:57,538
Thank you.

1108
01:07:58,263 --> 01:07:59,551
It's really nice of you to help us.

1109
01:08:00,050 --> 01:08:02,100
I wish I could do more
but we are moving out.

1110
01:08:02,459 --> 01:08:03,706
I am going with you.

1111
01:08:09,000 --> 01:08:11,650
Well, I just mean that we are going too.

1112
01:08:12,461 --> 01:08:13,032
Cool.

1113
01:08:13,057 --> 01:08:15,040
Tell that punk to shut the door.
We are out of here.

1114
01:08:15,450 --> 01:08:17,102
He can sniff around somewhere else.

1115
01:08:17,850 --> 01:08:18,844
Bye.
Bye.

1116
01:08:27,236 --> 01:08:30,386
It's Air Force One for crying out loud.
Still he gets sick.

1117
01:08:31,787 --> 01:08:34,137
I don't feel so good.
Look at me? Like a rock.

1118
01:08:34,700 --> 01:08:36,650
Could be bad weather could be
good weather. Doesn't matter.

1119
01:08:37,100 --> 01:08:39,520
We could go up, we could go down,
we could go back,

1120
01:08:39,544 --> 01:08:42,181
we could go forwards,
we could go side to side...

1121
01:08:45,117 --> 01:08:46,119
What did I say?

1122
01:08:49,000 --> 01:08:50,550
He still gets airsick?
Yeah.

1123
01:08:52,275 --> 01:08:53,875
Julius with all of this I...

1124
01:08:55,044 --> 01:08:57,144
I didn't get a chance to thank you two.

1125
01:08:58,700 --> 01:09:00,950
All he could think of was getting to you.

1126
01:09:04,182 --> 01:09:05,994
There is still love there I think.

1127
01:09:08,629 --> 01:09:10,303
Love was never a problem.

1128
01:09:11,006 --> 01:09:12,382
All you need is love.

1129
01:09:13,700 --> 01:09:14,512
John Lennon.

1130
01:09:14,671 --> 01:09:15,700
Smart man.

1131
01:09:15,900 --> 01:09:17,546
Shot in the back very sad.

1132
01:09:19,241 --> 01:09:22,941
We have moved as many of our forces
away from our bases as possible.

1133
01:09:23,060 --> 01:09:25,400
But we have already sustained heavy losses.

1134
01:09:25,425 --> 01:09:27,401
I spoke with the joint chiefs
when they arrived at NORAD.

1135
01:09:27,900 --> 01:09:31,700
They agree we must launch a counter
offensive with a full nuclear strike.

1136
01:09:31,850 --> 01:09:33,250
Over American soil?

1137
01:09:33,450 --> 01:09:37,237
You are saying at this point we should
sacrifice more innocent American civilians?

1138
01:09:37,238 --> 01:09:38,104
Is that right?

1139
01:09:38,148 --> 01:09:41,183
Sir, if we don't strike soon there may not
be much of an America left to defend!

1140
01:09:41,208 --> 01:09:41,765
Sir!

1141
01:09:41,886 --> 01:09:43,478
They have taken out NORAD!

1142
01:09:43,550 --> 01:09:45,085
What?
It's gone sir.

1143
01:09:45,568 --> 01:09:46,668
My God!

1144
01:09:47,700 --> 01:09:48,756
The vice president?

1145
01:09:48,886 --> 01:09:49,980
The joint chiefs?

1146
01:09:50,100 --> 01:09:51,150
Mr. President.

1147
01:09:53,116 --> 01:09:54,200
We must launch.

1148
01:09:54,400 --> 01:09:58,000
A delay now would be more costly than
when you waited to evacuate the cities.

1149
01:09:58,024 --> 01:10:00,524
No, no. You are not gonna
launch nuclear weapons!

1150
01:10:00,624 --> 01:10:02,598
You are gonna kill them and us at
the same time.

1151
01:10:02,622 --> 01:10:03,450
If we fire nukes...

1152
01:10:03,475 --> 01:10:05,084
then everybody else is going to fire them.
Sir may I remind you

1153
01:10:05,109 --> 01:10:06,059
You know what that means? Fallout!
You are a guest here.

1154
01:10:06,084 --> 01:10:07,498
You ever hear of nuclear winter?
David, you can't

1155
01:10:07,523 --> 01:10:09,076
It's the end of life as we know it.
Interfere with the conversation.

1156
01:10:09,101 --> 01:10:10,279
Do you hear what they are talking about?
I know I know.

1157
01:10:10,304 --> 01:10:11,204
Don't even think about it!
Just go.

1158
01:10:11,229 --> 01:10:12,318
I don't have to go.
You have to leave.

1159
01:10:12,343 --> 01:10:13,460
It can't be allowed!

1160
01:10:13,485 --> 01:10:15,074
Shut up! Captain get him out of here!

1161
01:10:15,098 --> 01:10:16,608
Hey, hey, don't tell him to shut up!

1162
01:10:17,943 --> 01:10:20,093
You'd all be dead now
if it was not for my David!

1163
01:10:21,735 --> 01:10:23,475
None of you did anything to prevent this!

1164
01:10:23,500 --> 01:10:24,910
There was nothing we could do.

1165
01:10:25,135 --> 01:10:27,174
We were totally unprepared for this.

1166
01:10:27,654 --> 01:10:29,554
Don't give me unprepared!
Come on Julius.

1167
01:10:29,579 --> 01:10:32,855
It was what? in the 1950s.
Whatever you had that spaceship.

1168
01:10:33,422 --> 01:10:34,668
Dad look Dad...

1169
01:10:34,692 --> 01:10:36,792
Yeah that thing that
you found in New Mexico!

1170
01:10:36,824 --> 01:10:37,933
Dad!
Where was that?

1171
01:10:37,958 --> 01:10:38,982
No, not the spaceship.

1172
01:10:39,007 --> 01:10:40,835
Roswell! Roswell New Mexico. Yeah!

1173
01:10:40,996 --> 01:10:43,405
No you had the spaceship
and you had the bodies!

1174
01:10:43,500 --> 01:10:45,500
They were locked up in a bunker.
Come on.

1175
01:10:45,525 --> 01:10:46,825
Where was that?
David?

1176
01:10:46,924 --> 01:10:48,400
I don't know.
Area 51! Right?

1177
01:10:48,425 --> 01:10:49,563
Area 51!

1178
01:10:49,796 --> 01:10:50,943
You knew then!

1179
01:10:51,162 --> 01:10:52,302
And you did nothing.

1180
01:10:53,282 --> 01:10:53,963
Sir.

1181
01:10:55,500 --> 01:10:58,150
Regardless of what you may
have read in the tabloids

1182
01:10:58,400 --> 01:11:00,184
there have never been any spacecraft

1183
01:11:00,409 --> 01:11:02,074
recovered by our government.

1184
01:11:02,308 --> 01:11:04,658
Take my word for it. There is no Area 51.

1185
01:11:05,150 --> 01:11:07,000
And there is no recovered spaceship.

1186
01:11:07,263 --> 01:11:08,757
Excuse me Mr. President.

1187
01:11:10,850 --> 01:11:14,200
That's not entirely accurate.

1188
01:11:19,400 --> 01:11:20,750
What? Which part?

1189
01:11:26,813 --> 01:11:29,009
Hold on everybody! Hold on!

1190
01:11:30,698 --> 01:11:31,548
Sorry.

1191
01:11:50,550 --> 01:11:52,100
The end hath come!

1192
01:11:52,490 --> 01:11:55,800
He speaketh His word
and the end hath come!

1193
01:11:55,950 --> 01:11:56,988
Hop on!

1194
01:11:57,313 --> 01:11:58,725
We are heading out to El Toro!

1195
01:11:59,850 --> 01:12:01,950
You cannot defy what hath come!

1196
01:12:03,250 --> 01:12:04,292
It is the end!

1197
01:12:10,950 --> 01:12:12,150
El Toro?

1198
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:21,950
Can you give me a hand?
Yeah sure.

1199
01:12:29,750 --> 01:12:30,800
Oh God!

1200
01:12:38,050 --> 01:12:38,831
Ok, ok.

1201
01:12:39,156 --> 01:12:40,268
Let's get this off.

1202
01:12:40,293 --> 01:12:41,443
Here, let me help you.

1203
01:12:45,625 --> 01:12:47,065
She is hurt pretty badly.

1204
01:12:51,402 --> 01:12:52,231
You know,

1205
01:12:52,574 --> 01:12:54,472
this was supposed to be my weekend off.

1206
01:12:56,020 --> 01:12:57,270
But nooo...

1207
01:12:58,000 --> 01:13:00,967
you got me out here
dragging your heavy ass,

1208
01:13:01,417 --> 01:13:02,880
through the burning desert,

1209
01:13:03,213 --> 01:13:05,732
with your dreadlocks sticking
out the back of my parachute.

1210
01:13:06,348 --> 01:13:08,448
You got to come down here
with an attitude,

1211
01:13:09,050 --> 01:13:10,731
acting all big and bad.

1212
01:13:13,200 --> 01:13:14,900
And what the hell is that smell?

1213
01:13:19,934 --> 01:13:21,689
I could have been at a barbecue!

1214
01:13:23,228 --> 01:13:24,494
But I ain't mad.

1215
01:13:25,000 --> 01:13:25,916
It's alright.

1216
01:13:26,622 --> 01:13:27,791
It's alright.

1217
01:13:43,450 --> 01:13:44,260
Hey!

1218
01:13:44,922 --> 01:13:45,617
Hey!

1219
01:13:46,437 --> 01:13:47,158
Hey!

1220
01:13:53,125 --> 01:13:54,000
Hey!

1221
01:14:07,457 --> 01:14:09,052
Do you need a lift soldier?

1222
01:14:09,911 --> 01:14:12,400
When I flew overhead
I saw a base not too far from here.

1223
01:14:15,498 --> 01:14:16,678
It ain't on the map.

1224
01:14:17,729 --> 01:14:18,861
Trust me it's there.

1225
01:14:35,450 --> 01:14:36,346
Ten hut!

1226
01:14:40,729 --> 01:14:41,987
Mr. President.
General.

1227
01:14:42,861 --> 01:14:44,120
Welcome to Area 51.

1228
01:14:44,747 --> 01:14:45,815
Please follow me.

1229
01:14:47,601 --> 01:14:49,850
We are now 24 floors beneath the surface

1230
01:14:50,100 --> 01:14:50,849
and...

1231
01:14:51,115 --> 01:14:52,789
here is our main research facility.

1232
01:14:53,183 --> 01:14:54,133
Let's see it.

1233
01:14:54,656 --> 01:14:56,063
I am sorry sir it's a clean room.

1234
01:14:56,087 --> 01:14:57,118
It's to keep it static free.

1235
01:14:57,143 --> 01:14:59,150
If we would all get to decontamination...
Open the door.

1236
01:15:01,386 --> 01:15:02,352
Yes sir.

1237
01:15:24,600 --> 01:15:25,750
My God!

1238
01:15:25,900 --> 01:15:28,000
Why the hell was not I told about this place?

1239
01:15:28,024 --> 01:15:29,304
Two words Mr. President.

1240
01:15:29,328 --> 01:15:31,245
Plausible deniability.

1241
01:15:39,339 --> 01:15:41,739
I don't understand.
Where does all this come from?

1242
01:15:41,764 --> 01:15:43,750
How do you get funding
for something like this?

1243
01:15:44,392 --> 01:15:47,164
You don't actually think
they spend $20000 on a hammer

1244
01:15:47,324 --> 01:15:49,474
$30000 on a toilet seat do you?

1245
01:15:51,798 --> 01:15:53,998
Mr. President, this is Dr. Okun.

1246
01:15:54,300 --> 01:15:56,361
He has been heading up the
research department on this...

1247
01:15:56,385 --> 01:15:58,350
project for the last 15 years.

1248
01:15:59,908 --> 01:16:01,151
How do you do?

1249
01:16:02,581 --> 01:16:03,816
Mr. President!

1250
01:16:07,250 --> 01:16:08,050
This...

1251
01:16:08,199 --> 01:16:09,199
What a pleasure!

1252
01:16:10,355 --> 01:16:11,755
As you can imagine they...

1253
01:16:12,672 --> 01:16:14,186
They don't let us out much.

1254
01:16:16,000 --> 01:16:17,186
I can understand that.

1255
01:16:19,450 --> 01:16:20,327
Well...

1256
01:16:21,353 --> 01:16:23,353
I guess you would like to see
the big Tamale?

1257
01:16:24,800 --> 01:16:25,746
Follow me.

1258
01:17:16,950 --> 01:17:18,528
She is a beaut ain't she?

1259
01:17:21,292 --> 01:17:22,871
As you can see from the repairs

1260
01:17:22,896 --> 01:17:26,272
we have been trying to put her back
together since the late 1960s.

1261
01:17:26,504 --> 01:17:29,754
Don't tell me you have had this for 40 years
and you don't know anything about them.

1262
01:17:30,100 --> 01:17:31,900
Oh hell no! No, no, no, no, no!

1263
01:17:31,925 --> 01:17:33,700
We know tons about them.

1264
01:17:34,486 --> 01:17:35,848
But, the neatest stuff...

1265
01:17:36,573 --> 01:17:39,250
The neatest stuff has only happened
in the last few days.

1266
01:17:39,600 --> 01:17:44,128
See we can't duplicate their type of power
so we have never been able to experiment.

1267
01:17:44,224 --> 01:17:45,955
But since these guys started showing up,

1268
01:17:45,979 --> 01:17:46,942
all the little...

1269
01:17:46,966 --> 01:17:49,024
gizmos inside turned on.

1270
01:17:50,521 --> 01:17:53,271
The last 24 hours have been really exciting!

1271
01:17:53,400 --> 01:17:54,324
Exciting?

1272
01:17:54,740 --> 01:17:56,083
People are dying out there.

1273
01:17:56,108 --> 01:17:58,608
I don't think exciting is the word
I would choose to describe it!

1274
01:18:00,800 --> 01:18:02,300
You guys are hoping to fly this thing?

1275
01:18:02,800 --> 01:18:04,700
You said you can repair their technology.

1276
01:18:04,900 --> 01:18:06,799
Can you tell us anything useful about them?

1277
01:18:06,824 --> 01:18:08,518
Oh yeah! Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1278
01:18:08,543 --> 01:18:09,713
Well I mean...

1279
01:18:09,825 --> 01:18:12,175
They are not all that dissimilar from us.

1280
01:18:12,557 --> 01:18:13,927
Breathes oxygen,

1281
01:18:13,951 --> 01:18:16,425
comparable tolerances to heat, cold.

1282
01:18:16,859 --> 01:18:18,959
Probably why they are interested in our planet.

1283
01:18:20,201 --> 01:18:21,003
Hey!

1284
01:18:21,742 --> 01:18:22,503
Hey!

1285
01:18:25,144 --> 01:18:26,465
You guys wanna see them?

1286
01:18:36,650 --> 01:18:37,850
This is...

1287
01:18:38,151 --> 01:18:39,431
This is the vault.

1288
01:18:40,635 --> 01:18:41,455
Or as...

1289
01:18:41,720 --> 01:18:43,243
some of us have come to call it...

1290
01:18:44,100 --> 01:18:45,500
the freak show.

1291
01:19:08,422 --> 01:19:09,672
When we found them

1292
01:19:10,300 --> 01:19:11,401
they were wearing...

1293
01:19:11,425 --> 01:19:12,270
some sort of...

1294
01:19:12,350 --> 01:19:13,929
bio-mechanical suits.

1295
01:19:14,226 --> 01:19:17,726
Once we got them off, we learned
a great deal about their anatomy.

1296
01:19:18,085 --> 01:19:19,685
Eyes, ears

1297
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:21,175
no vocal cords.

1298
01:19:21,309 --> 01:19:24,988
We are assuming they communicate
with each other through some other means.

1299
01:19:25,259 --> 01:19:26,917
You are obviously not thinking about...

1300
01:19:26,941 --> 01:19:28,659
hand signals and body language.

1301
01:19:29,320 --> 01:19:32,770
It's some kind of extrasensory
perception telepathy.

1302
01:19:34,300 --> 01:19:35,300
So...

1303
01:19:37,600 --> 01:19:39,407
It's an organic life form.

1304
01:19:42,900 --> 01:19:43,952
Can they be killed?

1305
01:19:44,304 --> 01:19:46,483
Their bodies are just as frail as ours.

1306
01:19:46,536 --> 01:19:48,616
And these two died in the crash.

1307
01:19:49,200 --> 01:19:50,686
This one a few weeks later.

1308
01:19:51,100 --> 01:19:52,000
You just...

1309
01:19:52,425 --> 01:19:55,224
You have to get through their
technology which is...

1310
01:19:55,650 --> 01:19:56,738
I am sorry to say...

1311
01:19:57,293 --> 01:19:58,611
far more advanced.

1312
01:19:59,793 --> 01:20:00,618
David

1313
01:20:01,400 --> 01:20:03,474
you unlocked part of their technology.

1314
01:20:03,700 --> 01:20:04,900
You cracked the code.

1315
01:20:04,924 --> 01:20:06,700
Oh, no, no.
All I did was stumble onto their...

1316
01:20:08,120 --> 01:20:09,580
signal. I don't know how...

1317
01:20:09,821 --> 01:20:11,060
helpful I can be.

1318
01:20:11,900 --> 01:20:14,350
Why don't you show him
what you have discovered so far?

1319
01:20:15,646 --> 01:20:17,646
Figure out what they have not thought of yet.

1320
01:20:19,225 --> 01:20:22,325
We will see if you are as smart
as we all hope you are.

1321
01:20:33,550 --> 01:20:34,800
What code?

1322
01:20:55,300 --> 01:20:57,700
Captain Steven Hiller
United States Marine Corps.

1323
01:20:58,000 --> 01:20:59,648
I am sorry captain.
This is a restricted area.

1324
01:20:59,792 --> 01:21:01,324
I can't let you pass without clearance.

1325
01:21:02,148 --> 01:21:02,948
Ok.

1326
01:21:03,309 --> 01:21:04,309
Come here.

1327
01:21:04,900 --> 01:21:06,100
You wanna see my clearance?

1328
01:21:09,658 --> 01:21:11,326
Maybe I will just leave this here with you.

1329
01:21:12,108 --> 01:21:13,089
Let them pass.

1330
01:21:13,356 --> 01:21:15,006
Let them pass!
Get the hell out of the way!

1331
01:21:17,950 --> 01:21:19,200
Did you see that?

1332
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:21,463
Come on down.
Look!

1333
01:21:22,480 --> 01:21:23,658
Watch your step.
Alright.

1334
01:21:23,683 --> 01:21:24,370
Yeah.

1335
01:21:24,979 --> 01:21:26,286
Well obviously this...

1336
01:21:26,440 --> 01:21:28,695
this cockpit
was designed to seat three.

1337
01:21:28,935 --> 01:21:31,585
Though, how they sat on them
I don't know.

1338
01:21:32,150 --> 01:21:32,850
Gently.

1339
01:21:33,742 --> 01:21:35,718
You see these gizmos flashing?
Yeah.

1340
01:21:36,289 --> 01:21:39,164
We have been working around the clock
trying to get a fix on all this crap.

1341
01:21:39,500 --> 01:21:41,400
Some stuff we figured out right away.

1342
01:21:41,998 --> 01:21:43,386
This we are pretty sure,

1343
01:21:43,410 --> 01:21:45,648
is the life support system for the cabin.

1344
01:21:46,700 --> 01:21:49,000
And this doohickey is connected to...

1345
01:21:50,404 --> 01:21:51,061
Well it...

1346
01:21:51,686 --> 01:21:53,647
was connected to the engine.

1347
01:21:53,671 --> 01:21:55,002
Here take that will you?

1348
01:21:56,450 --> 01:21:58,250
These configurations...

1349
01:22:01,450 --> 01:22:03,281
Well, to be honest we, we-we...

1350
01:22:03,523 --> 01:22:05,418
don't know what the hell this crap is.

1351
01:22:06,250 --> 01:22:06,993
But this...

1352
01:22:07,017 --> 01:22:09,537
is clearly what they use to...

1353
01:22:09,561 --> 01:22:11,550
guide and navigate their craft.

1354
01:22:12,314 --> 01:22:13,134
Neat?

1355
01:22:14,553 --> 01:22:16,045
Somebody could grab my laptop there?

1356
01:22:16,070 --> 01:22:17,462
Doc can I just, can I just have the...

1357
01:22:18,124 --> 01:22:19,374
computer inside.
What?

1358
01:22:19,399 --> 01:22:21,383
See these patterns here,
they are repeating sequentially,

1359
01:22:21,407 --> 01:22:22,882
just like their countdown signal.

1360
01:22:23,300 --> 01:22:25,720
They are using that frequency
for computer communications.

1361
01:22:26,700 --> 01:22:28,665
See?
That's how they are coordinating their ships.

1362
01:22:30,027 --> 01:22:30,868
You know...

1363
01:22:32,150 --> 01:22:33,800
You are really starting
to make us look bad.

1364
01:22:42,250 --> 01:22:43,363
They got one!

1365
01:22:43,699 --> 01:22:45,012
They got one alive!

1366
01:22:45,050 --> 01:22:46,241
They got one alive!

1367
01:22:46,265 --> 01:22:47,450
Jesus!
Look.

1368
01:22:48,036 --> 01:22:49,546
You will be ok by yourself Dave?

1369
01:22:50,000 --> 01:22:51,179
Fine by it.
Yeah.

1370
01:22:51,400 --> 01:22:53,000
Don't touch anything.

1371
01:22:55,300 --> 01:22:57,400
Everybody is always telling me
not to touch anything.

1372
01:22:58,900 --> 01:23:00,300
Here, here.

1373
01:23:02,388 --> 01:23:03,588
It's all wet.

1374
01:23:13,834 --> 01:23:15,734
Right here.
We got him in the back of the pickup.

1375
01:23:20,400 --> 01:23:23,200
General sir. Captain Steven Hiller
United States Marine Corps.

1376
01:23:24,357 --> 01:23:25,854
Guess who is coming to dinner!

1377
01:23:26,401 --> 01:23:27,722
I need a doctor.

1378
01:23:28,662 --> 01:23:30,090
I need a doctor!

1379
01:23:32,650 --> 01:23:33,455
Oh boy!

1380
01:23:33,698 --> 01:23:35,656
Oh boy!
How long has he been unconscious?

1381
01:23:35,681 --> 01:23:37,578
About three hours.
Let's get him in containment stat!

1382
01:23:37,603 --> 01:23:39,544
My son, he is very sick.

1383
01:23:39,763 --> 01:23:41,198
He needs immediate attention!

1384
01:23:41,649 --> 01:23:42,672
He is drying out.

1385
01:23:42,821 --> 01:23:44,225
I want him sprayed down with saline.

1386
01:23:44,250 --> 01:23:46,075
He has a problem with his adrenal cortex.

1387
01:23:46,748 --> 01:23:47,639
Please!

1388
01:23:50,400 --> 01:23:53,326
If you don't do something about it
right now my son will die!

1389
01:23:53,834 --> 01:23:54,896
Ok just help him!

1390
01:23:55,076 --> 01:23:55,769
Ok.

1391
01:23:55,793 --> 01:23:57,574
O'Haver, Miller you come with us.

1392
01:23:57,700 --> 01:23:59,458
You, take us to him, ok?

1393
01:23:59,595 --> 01:24:00,386
Let's go.

1394
01:24:03,100 --> 01:24:04,600
Alright! Move it, move it, move it!

1395
01:24:05,949 --> 01:24:08,114
As the former head of the CIA,

1396
01:24:08,138 --> 01:24:09,498
you knew about this place.

1397
01:24:09,600 --> 01:24:11,800
When were you planning
on informing the rest of us?

1398
01:24:11,900 --> 01:24:13,800
It had been deemed classified.

1399
01:24:13,824 --> 01:24:16,300
You should have told us about
this when they first arrived!

1400
01:24:16,900 --> 01:24:19,650
You should have warned us
before we launched a counterattack

1401
01:24:19,675 --> 01:24:22,357
that cost the lives of hundreds
of American pilots!

1402
01:24:22,382 --> 01:24:23,749
There was no way that we could have known

1403
01:24:23,774 --> 01:24:25,874
that our fighters would have been
that ineffective against their attackers.

1404
01:24:26,750 --> 01:24:27,900
Mr. President.

1405
01:24:27,925 --> 01:24:30,825
The little bit of information we have comes
directly into this room Mr. President.

1406
01:24:31,950 --> 01:24:34,300
Atlanta, Chicago and Philadelphia.

1407
01:24:35,123 --> 01:24:36,174
Destroyed.

1408
01:24:36,556 --> 01:24:39,729
We learned that NATO and Western Allied
installations...

1409
01:24:40,057 --> 01:24:41,666
were the first to be taken out.

1410
01:24:41,975 --> 01:24:42,979
Then we were hit.

1411
01:24:43,275 --> 01:24:46,213
They knew exactly where and how to hit us.

1412
01:24:46,238 --> 01:24:48,861
And our forces?
We are down to 15%.

1413
01:24:49,280 --> 01:24:53,593
If you calculate the time it takes
to destroy a city and move on

1414
01:24:53,618 --> 01:24:56,162
we are looking at the worldwide
destruction...

1415
01:24:56,529 --> 01:24:58,161
of every major city...

1416
01:24:59,090 --> 01:25:00,125
in the next...

1417
01:25:00,149 --> 01:25:01,740
36 hours.

1418
01:25:03,457 --> 01:25:05,207
We are being exterminated.

1419
01:25:09,200 --> 01:25:10,300
Mr. President.

1420
01:25:11,312 --> 01:25:12,712
This is Captain Steven Hiller.

1421
01:25:13,400 --> 01:25:14,800
Captain.
Mr. President.

1422
01:25:14,950 --> 01:25:16,000
Well done!

1423
01:25:16,600 --> 01:25:17,752
Where is it now?

1424
01:25:17,777 --> 01:25:19,877
We have it isolated down
in the containment lab sir.

1425
01:25:21,198 --> 01:25:22,334
I would like to go see it.

1426
01:25:28,200 --> 01:25:28,987
General,

1427
01:25:29,221 --> 01:25:31,660
I am really anxious
to get back to El Toro.

1428
01:25:34,250 --> 01:25:35,770
Has not anyone told you?

1429
01:25:39,424 --> 01:25:41,590
El Toro has been completely destroyed.

1430
01:26:34,606 --> 01:26:36,096
We were lucky.
Yeah!

1431
01:26:37,004 --> 01:26:39,004
Today was the first time I used the subway.

1432
01:26:39,850 --> 01:26:41,800
Thank God for the Metro Rail.

1433
01:26:42,501 --> 01:26:43,953
These should last us a while.

1434
01:26:44,500 --> 01:26:46,550
Don't move. I will get it for you.
Stay still.

1435
01:26:48,782 --> 01:26:49,953
He is your son?

1436
01:26:51,277 --> 01:26:52,565
He is my angel.

1437
01:26:53,690 --> 01:26:55,300
Was his father stationed here?

1438
01:26:56,100 --> 01:26:57,400
No he...

1439
01:26:58,250 --> 01:26:59,573
He was not his father.

1440
01:27:01,500 --> 01:27:03,931
But I was kind of hoping
he wanted the job though.

1441
01:27:08,650 --> 01:27:10,330
So what do you do for a living?

1442
01:27:10,951 --> 01:27:11,961
I am a dancer.

1443
01:27:12,964 --> 01:27:14,014
Ballet!

1444
01:27:14,800 --> 01:27:15,550
No.

1445
01:27:16,675 --> 01:27:17,623
Exotic.

1446
01:27:21,401 --> 01:27:22,261
Sorry.

1447
01:27:22,437 --> 01:27:23,401
Don't be.

1448
01:27:24,120 --> 01:27:25,104
I am not.

1449
01:27:25,350 --> 01:27:26,271
It's good money.

1450
01:27:26,629 --> 01:27:27,434
Besides...

1451
01:27:27,683 --> 01:27:29,050
My baby is worth it.

1452
01:27:29,209 --> 01:27:29,983
Dylan.

1453
01:27:30,280 --> 01:27:31,083
Come here.

1454
01:27:31,868 --> 01:27:33,632
I want you to meet the First Lady.

1455
01:27:37,529 --> 01:27:39,129
Hello.
Hi.

1456
01:27:40,500 --> 01:27:42,709
I didn't know that you would recognized me.

1457
01:27:42,780 --> 01:27:44,830
Well, I didn't want to say nothing.

1458
01:27:45,481 --> 01:27:47,241
I voted for the other guy.

1459
01:27:49,766 --> 01:27:51,899
Alright life support monitors recording.

1460
01:27:51,979 --> 01:27:53,797
So if we screw up, it's all on tape.

1461
01:27:53,822 --> 01:27:55,624
Ok, come on, come on, come on.

1462
01:27:55,678 --> 01:27:57,454
Let's get this bio mechanical suit off.

1463
01:27:57,975 --> 01:27:59,304
Put the spreader right here,

1464
01:27:59,428 --> 01:28:00,525
right along the ridge.

1465
01:28:00,550 --> 01:28:02,849
Microprobe thingamajig goes right here.

1466
01:28:03,138 --> 01:28:04,568
Pick there. Good.

1467
01:28:05,043 --> 01:28:06,102
Alright now spread it,

1468
01:28:06,126 --> 01:28:07,771
very, very gently.

1469
01:28:07,864 --> 01:28:08,914
Let me get in.

1470
01:28:16,050 --> 01:28:18,100
Gentle, gentle that's it.

1471
01:28:19,389 --> 01:28:21,589
Run this right, in...

1472
01:28:27,500 --> 01:28:28,750
Alright. Ok.

1473
01:28:29,396 --> 01:28:30,796
Let's proceed.

1474
01:28:31,050 --> 01:28:32,420
Now comes the...

1475
01:28:32,667 --> 01:28:34,500
the really icky part.

1476
01:28:36,462 --> 01:28:37,563
Oh boy!

1477
01:28:38,287 --> 01:28:40,053
This is one, smelly...

1478
01:28:40,638 --> 01:28:41,883
disgusting.

1479
01:28:50,350 --> 01:28:51,450
Oh look at it!

1480
01:28:52,290 --> 01:28:54,060
It doesn't look alive does it?

1481
01:28:58,250 --> 01:29:00,100
The arm is moving.

1482
01:29:09,850 --> 01:29:11,125
Doctor?

1483
01:29:14,950 --> 01:29:16,295
Doctor? Doctor?

1484
01:29:18,856 --> 01:29:20,004
Don't move! Don't move!

1485
01:29:21,434 --> 01:29:22,544
Oh my god!

1486
01:30:05,618 --> 01:30:06,834
Dr. Okun?

1487
01:30:29,956 --> 01:30:31,497
<i>Release...</i>

1488
01:30:31,864 --> 01:30:33,073
<i>me.</i>

1489
01:30:33,441 --> 01:30:35,641
Open the door. Get him out of there!
No wait.

1490
01:30:50,250 --> 01:30:52,040
<i>Release me</i>

1491
01:30:52,900 --> 01:30:54,001
<i>now.</i>

1492
01:30:56,415 --> 01:30:58,884
<i>Now!</i>

1493
01:31:05,250 --> 01:31:07,921
<i>I know there is much
we can learn from each other</i>

1494
01:31:08,000 --> 01:31:10,226
<i>if we can negotiate a truce.</i>

1495
01:31:11,300 --> 01:31:13,700
<i>We can find a way to coexist.</i>

1496
01:31:15,745 --> 01:31:18,295
<i>Can there be a peace between us?</i>

1497
01:31:18,800 --> 01:31:20,668
<i>Peace?</i>

1498
01:31:22,300 --> 01:31:24,600
<i>No peace.</i>

1499
01:31:30,681 --> 01:31:32,522
<i>What is it you want us to do?</i>

1500
01:31:34,950 --> 01:31:36,850
<i>Die.</i>

1501
01:31:46,100 --> 01:31:48,621
<i>Die!</i>

1502
01:31:50,458 --> 01:31:51,247
Sir!

1503
01:31:52,950 --> 01:31:54,000
Mr. President.

1504
01:31:55,600 --> 01:31:57,832
Is that glass bulletproof?
No sir.

1505
01:32:17,800 --> 01:32:19,574
Are you alright?
I saw...

1506
01:32:20,360 --> 01:32:21,582
his thoughts.

1507
01:32:22,650 --> 01:32:24,361
I saw what they are planning to do.

1508
01:32:27,000 --> 01:32:28,493
They are like locusts.

1509
01:32:29,550 --> 01:32:31,550
They are moving from planet to planet.

1510
01:32:31,750 --> 01:32:33,196
Their whole civilization.

1511
01:32:34,000 --> 01:32:37,250
After they ave consumed every
natural resource they move on.

1512
01:32:39,650 --> 01:32:41,084
And we are next.

1513
01:32:53,000 --> 01:32:54,153
Nuke them.

1514
01:32:55,900 --> 01:32:57,557
Let's nuke the bastards.

1515
01:33:09,300 --> 01:33:11,101
Just my luck. No ice.

1516
01:33:12,491 --> 01:33:13,952
I take it you have heard?

1517
01:33:15,575 --> 01:33:16,692
Hey toast.

1518
01:33:18,200 --> 01:33:19,325
To the end of the world.

1519
01:33:19,707 --> 01:33:21,750
He didn't come to this decision lightly.

1520
01:33:22,298 --> 01:33:24,082
He didn't have any other choice.

1521
01:33:25,050 --> 01:33:27,050
Well, you still believe in him.

1522
01:33:27,200 --> 01:33:29,150
Yeah.
Well he is a good man.

1523
01:33:31,050 --> 01:33:32,094
He would better be.

1524
01:33:32,425 --> 01:33:33,990
You left me for him or...

1525
01:33:34,270 --> 01:33:36,288
you know, for your career.

1526
01:33:36,565 --> 01:33:38,100
You know it was not just my...

1527
01:33:38,351 --> 01:33:39,167
career.

1528
01:33:39,356 --> 01:33:41,806
It was the biggest opportunity of my life.

1529
01:33:42,253 --> 01:33:46,050
I wanted my life to make a difference.
I wanted my life to mean something.

1530
01:33:46,075 --> 01:33:47,375
Yeah. And...

1531
01:33:47,975 --> 01:33:49,274
I was not...

1532
01:33:49,700 --> 01:33:50,790
ambitious...

1533
01:33:51,114 --> 01:33:52,000
David!
Enough for you?

1534
01:33:52,025 --> 01:33:53,825
David you could have done
anything that you wanted.

1535
01:33:54,014 --> 01:33:56,160
Research development...
Oh honey,

1536
01:33:56,184 --> 01:33:57,614
I was happy where I was.

1537
01:33:58,092 --> 01:34:00,842
Have not you ever wanted to be
part of something special?

1538
01:34:04,400 --> 01:34:05,967
I was part of something special.

1539
01:34:21,850 --> 01:34:23,652
Well if it makes any difference

1540
01:34:23,797 --> 01:34:25,527
I never stopped loving you.

1541
01:34:27,450 --> 01:34:28,931
But that was not enough was it?

1542
01:34:48,050 --> 01:34:50,100
Let's pick it up man. We have got
a tight schedule. Now let's go!

1543
01:34:57,479 --> 01:34:59,679
Let's pick it up man.
We are on a tight schedule. Let's go!

1544
01:34:59,774 --> 01:35:00,707
Let's go man!

1545
01:35:01,612 --> 01:35:02,715
Pick it up!

1546
01:35:06,827 --> 01:35:08,933
What the hell are you doing?
Get out of there!

1547
01:35:10,417 --> 01:35:12,721
Look I got something I got to handle.
I am just borrowing it.

1548
01:35:12,746 --> 01:35:13,946
No you are not sir.

1549
01:35:14,550 --> 01:35:15,987
Do you really wanna shoot me?

1550
01:35:18,750 --> 01:35:20,291
Just tell them I hit you.

1551
01:35:26,674 --> 01:35:28,474
Command this is Retal Op.

1552
01:35:28,499 --> 01:35:29,627
Squadron is in the air.

1553
01:35:29,652 --> 01:35:30,620
We are on station

1554
01:35:30,645 --> 01:35:31,853
<i>and awaiting instructions.</i>

1555
01:35:31,878 --> 01:35:34,306
Roger. Break formation.
Head to targets.

1556
01:35:39,400 --> 01:35:40,204
Sir...

1557
01:35:40,902 --> 01:35:42,032
They are breaking formation.

1558
01:35:42,700 --> 01:35:45,019
Mr. President we are
initiating sequence code.

1559
01:35:45,043 --> 01:35:47,300
Alpha. Zulu. Six. Eight. Niner.

1560
01:35:47,611 --> 01:35:49,261
Which city will be reached first?

1561
01:35:49,459 --> 01:35:50,740
Houston Texas.

1562
01:35:50,910 --> 01:35:52,775
ETA six minutes and counting down.

1563
01:35:52,800 --> 01:35:53,706
Houston.

1564
01:35:53,731 --> 01:35:55,775
The major cities have been deserted.

1565
01:35:55,917 --> 01:35:59,520
Civilian casualties should
be down to a minimum.

1566
01:36:03,202 --> 01:36:04,822
Command this is Neighborhood Watch.

1567
01:36:05,750 --> 01:36:07,040
We are in position.

1568
01:36:07,500 --> 01:36:09,550
Tracking monitors are locked on.

1569
01:36:09,700 --> 01:36:12,100
We are going to visual recon.

1570
01:36:12,600 --> 01:36:13,967
<i>Roger that TC.</i>

1571
01:36:18,300 --> 01:36:19,437
We have confirmation.

1572
01:36:19,562 --> 01:36:20,974
Launch code confirmed.

1573
01:36:20,999 --> 01:36:23,633
Alpha. Zulu. Six. Eight. Niner. Standing by.

1574
01:36:27,100 --> 01:36:28,100
Laser targeting.

1575
01:36:29,826 --> 01:36:30,953
Locked on.

1576
01:36:31,750 --> 01:36:32,982
We are locked on sir.

1577
01:36:33,253 --> 01:36:34,653
Do you wish to deploy?

1578
01:36:38,550 --> 01:36:41,800
Mr. President if you wish to deploy
the time is now.

1579
01:36:48,500 --> 01:36:50,300
Mr. President?
Deploy.

1580
01:36:50,550 --> 01:36:53,300
That's a go. Alpha. Zulu. Six. Eight. Niner.
That's correct. Deploy.

1581
01:36:53,500 --> 01:36:54,900
Here we go.

1582
01:37:03,384 --> 01:37:04,470
Bird is away.

1583
01:37:04,495 --> 01:37:06,295
We have visual confirmation of the missile.

1584
01:37:06,990 --> 01:37:08,190
It's on target.

1585
01:37:08,679 --> 01:37:09,679
<i>Approaching.</i>

1586
01:37:11,000 --> 01:37:12,585
May our children forgive us.

1587
01:37:12,610 --> 01:37:13,941
<i>Five seconds to impact.</i>

1588
01:37:14,266 --> 01:37:15,025
<i>Three.</i>

1589
01:37:15,384 --> 01:37:16,219
<i>Two.</i>

1590
01:37:16,450 --> 01:37:17,180
One.

1591
01:37:19,700 --> 01:37:21,550
Oh yeah! It's a hit!

1592
01:37:26,250 --> 01:37:28,330
Get down! Get down!

1593
01:37:29,182 --> 01:37:31,300
Can we confirm that
the target was destroyed?

1594
01:37:31,575 --> 01:37:34,285
Get the tank commander on line. I want
confirmation that the target was destroyed.

1595
01:37:34,310 --> 01:37:35,121
Yes sir!

1596
01:37:35,146 --> 01:37:37,692
Red Arrow Alpha 9723. Can you read?

1597
01:37:38,950 --> 01:37:40,500
Repeat Commander.
You are breaking up.

1598
01:37:40,925 --> 01:37:41,974
<i>We have lost visual.</i>

1599
01:37:42,100 --> 01:37:43,700
Roger that.
We are looking for confirmation.

1600
01:37:51,650 --> 01:37:53,540
We got the bastards.
Yeah!

1601
01:37:53,700 --> 01:37:55,550
Good job everyone! Congratulations!

1602
01:37:57,802 --> 01:37:59,278
Commander do you have visual?

1603
01:37:59,302 --> 01:38:01,643
I repeat we need visual confirmation.

1604
01:38:01,890 --> 01:38:03,619
Has the target been destroyed?

1605
01:38:18,000 --> 01:38:19,100
Negative.

1606
01:38:21,975 --> 01:38:23,193
<i>Target remains.</i>

1607
01:38:26,451 --> 01:38:27,431
<i>I repeat,</i>

1608
01:38:28,166 --> 01:38:29,834
<i>target remains.</i>

1609
01:38:34,013 --> 01:38:35,560
Call the other planes back.

1610
01:38:36,082 --> 01:38:39,325
Other bombers might have more luck.
We should not just give up on this!

1611
01:38:39,350 --> 01:38:41,150
I said call them back!

1612
01:38:44,200 --> 01:38:45,032
Abort.

1613
01:38:45,651 --> 01:38:46,600
Abort mission.

1614
01:38:46,624 --> 01:38:48,068
Issue the abort codes right away.

1615
01:38:48,092 --> 01:38:50,224
This is an abort, full abort.
Do you read?

1616
01:38:50,666 --> 01:38:51,873
Abort mission right away.

1617
01:39:30,000 --> 01:39:30,946
Jasmine!

1618
01:39:44,100 --> 01:39:45,154
You are late!

1619
01:39:45,900 --> 01:39:47,815
You know I like to make an entrance.

1620
01:39:57,640 --> 01:39:59,640
Where are we going?
Through there sir.

1621
01:40:00,276 --> 01:40:03,626
Mr. President your wife is resting
comfortably for the moment.

1622
01:40:03,651 --> 01:40:06,951
Perhaps if we had gotten to her earlier...
Hey, hey, there she is! Go on!

1623
01:40:10,600 --> 01:40:13,595
She doesn't look too good.
Your wife is bleeding internally Mr. President.

1624
01:40:14,398 --> 01:40:17,400
Perhaps if we had got her earlier...
Wait a minute. What are you saying?

1625
01:40:18,800 --> 01:40:20,147
We can't stop the bleeding.

1626
01:40:21,550 --> 01:40:22,650
If we had...

1627
01:40:23,800 --> 01:40:25,390
There is nothing we can do for her.

1628
01:40:27,100 --> 01:40:29,557
We were worried.
We didn't know where you were.

1629
01:40:35,800 --> 01:40:37,607
You have gotten bigger I think.

1630
01:40:37,900 --> 01:40:38,951
I did?

1631
01:40:42,150 --> 01:40:44,121
You just keep growing and growing.

1632
01:40:46,700 --> 01:40:47,652
I can't...

1633
01:40:49,720 --> 01:40:50,512
Hey.

1634
01:40:51,500 --> 01:40:52,367
Can you...

1635
01:40:52,707 --> 01:40:55,423
wait outside for a little bit
so mom can get a rest?

1636
01:40:56,173 --> 01:40:57,673
Hey come on Munchkin.

1637
01:41:07,250 --> 01:41:10,850
I am so sorry that I didn't come home
when you asked me to.

1638
01:41:13,764 --> 01:41:14,562
It's ok.

1639
01:41:17,634 --> 01:41:18,928
The doctors...

1640
01:41:20,400 --> 01:41:21,850
think that you are...

1641
01:41:22,336 --> 01:41:23,756
gonna be just fine.

1642
01:41:27,150 --> 01:41:28,250
Liar.

1643
01:42:25,509 --> 01:42:27,193
Is Mommy sleeping now?

1644
01:42:29,300 --> 01:42:30,073
Yeah.

1645
01:42:32,150 --> 01:42:33,573
Mommy is sleeping.

1646
01:42:37,600 --> 01:42:38,600
Hey.

1647
01:43:10,100 --> 01:43:10,964
David!

1648
01:43:11,700 --> 01:43:12,956
What the hell are you doing?

1649
01:43:13,024 --> 01:43:14,294
I am making a mess!

1650
01:43:14,900 --> 01:43:16,450
Yeah. This I can see.

1651
01:43:16,600 --> 01:43:19,250
We got to burn the rainforest
with toxic waste

1652
01:43:19,275 --> 01:43:21,525
pollute the air and rip up the ozone layer!

1653
01:43:21,800 --> 01:43:23,850
Because maybe if we screw
this planet up enough.

1654
01:43:25,400 --> 01:43:27,000
They won't want it anymore.

1655
01:43:27,550 --> 01:43:29,150
Wait, wait, wait. David. David!

1656
01:43:29,175 --> 01:43:30,340
Don't do this to yourself.

1657
01:43:30,511 --> 01:43:31,368
Listen to me.

1658
01:43:31,529 --> 01:43:32,829
Listen to me.
I am listening.

1659
01:43:33,450 --> 01:43:35,724
Everyone loses faith
at some point in their life.

1660
01:43:35,875 --> 01:43:37,625
David. Even myself.

1661
01:43:39,336 --> 01:43:41,786
I have not spoken to God
since your mother died.

1662
01:43:48,345 --> 01:43:49,548
You see sometimes...

1663
01:43:50,217 --> 01:43:52,092
we have to remember what we still have.

1664
01:43:53,733 --> 01:43:54,678
Like what?

1665
01:43:58,050 --> 01:43:58,913
Well...

1666
01:43:59,842 --> 01:44:01,202
you still have your health.

1667
01:44:03,137 --> 01:44:05,387
Come on. David. David. you need your rest.
Come on!

1668
01:44:05,600 --> 01:44:08,450
Get off this freezing concrete floor
before you catch a cold. Come on.

1669
01:44:11,723 --> 01:44:12,847
What did you just say?

1670
01:44:13,299 --> 01:44:14,371
You mean about faith?

1671
01:44:14,550 --> 01:44:15,195
Well,

1672
01:44:15,332 --> 01:44:17,150
you see a man can live his life...
No, no, no.

1673
01:44:17,174 --> 01:44:18,350
No, the other part.

1674
01:44:18,969 --> 01:44:19,934
What? What?

1675
01:44:20,394 --> 01:44:21,674
I don't want you to catch cold.

1676
01:44:27,050 --> 01:44:28,750
What is that?
What's the matter with you?

1677
01:44:29,600 --> 01:44:30,600
Genius.

1678
01:44:31,816 --> 01:44:32,659
Genius?

1679
01:44:32,935 --> 01:44:33,797
My dad.

1680
01:44:34,165 --> 01:44:35,284
A total genius.

1681
01:44:37,350 --> 01:44:38,090
Jerry?

1682
01:44:38,315 --> 01:44:39,214
Wake up.

1683
01:44:39,350 --> 01:44:41,450
We got work to do.
Get everybody down here, right away.

1684
01:44:43,339 --> 01:44:44,089
What?

1685
01:44:47,174 --> 01:44:48,175
Look at that!

1686
01:44:49,000 --> 01:44:51,700
Does that thing really fly in outer space?

1687
01:44:51,800 --> 01:44:53,344
It most certainly does.

1688
01:44:53,674 --> 01:44:55,133
Sure doesn't look like it.

1689
01:44:55,437 --> 01:44:56,375
Hey, they are here.

1690
01:44:56,666 --> 01:44:58,375
Alright Connie what's this all about?

1691
01:44:58,925 --> 01:45:00,125
I have no idea.

1692
01:45:00,150 --> 01:45:01,211
Get everybody off.

1693
01:45:01,236 --> 01:45:02,868
Right everybody. Clear the platform.

1694
01:45:02,892 --> 01:45:04,048
Come on. Come on.

1695
01:45:05,230 --> 01:45:06,230
Major Mitchell...

1696
01:45:06,570 --> 01:45:08,165
Do you have a pistol?
What?

1697
01:45:08,450 --> 01:45:10,243
You got a gun?
Sergeant your sidearm.

1698
01:45:13,000 --> 01:45:13,920
See that...

1699
01:45:14,231 --> 01:45:16,300
Coke can on top of the alien craft?

1700
01:45:16,400 --> 01:45:17,833
Think you can shoot that thing off?

1701
01:45:18,565 --> 01:45:19,614
Do it. Shoot it.

1702
01:45:20,100 --> 01:45:20,833
Sir?

1703
01:45:22,578 --> 01:45:23,472
Go ahead.

1704
01:45:29,900 --> 01:45:31,100
What the hell are you doing?

1705
01:45:31,150 --> 01:45:32,164
I am sorry. My fault.

1706
01:45:32,642 --> 01:45:33,586
My-My fault.

1707
01:45:33,611 --> 01:45:34,691
That Coke can...

1708
01:45:35,001 --> 01:45:36,749
was protected by the craft's shield.

1709
01:45:36,774 --> 01:45:38,006
We can't penetrate their defenses.

1710
01:45:38,031 --> 01:45:39,564
We know that already.
What's your point?

1711
01:45:39,675 --> 01:45:41,814
Right. My point is
if we can't beat their defenses

1712
01:45:42,264 --> 01:45:43,660
then we got to get around them.

1713
01:45:43,715 --> 01:45:46,183
Major one more time...

1714
01:45:46,550 --> 01:45:47,774
Any time.

1715
01:45:58,800 --> 01:45:59,938
How did you do that?

1716
01:46:00,663 --> 01:46:01,924
I gave it a cold.

1717
01:46:03,132 --> 01:46:04,257
I gave it a virus.

1718
01:46:04,984 --> 01:46:06,708
A computer virus.

1719
01:46:07,350 --> 01:46:09,671
Are you telling us you can send out a signal

1720
01:46:09,800 --> 01:46:11,800
that will disable all their shields?

1721
01:46:11,824 --> 01:46:14,100
That's right. Just like they
used our satellites against us.

1722
01:46:14,524 --> 01:46:16,108
We can use their own signal...

1723
01:46:16,351 --> 01:46:17,469
against them.

1724
01:46:17,600 --> 01:46:19,236
If we plant a virus,

1725
01:46:19,550 --> 01:46:20,808
into that mother ship

1726
01:46:20,924 --> 01:46:23,650
it's gonna then filter down into
all the corresponding ships below.

1727
01:46:24,661 --> 01:46:26,049
I am sorry. I don't understand.

1728
01:46:26,074 --> 01:46:30,500
Just how exactly do we infect the
mother ship with this virus?

1729
01:46:31,400 --> 01:46:33,924
We are... We are gonna...

1730
01:46:34,626 --> 01:46:35,588
have to...

1731
01:46:36,263 --> 01:46:39,075
fly their alien craft out of our
atmosphere and dock with it.

1732
01:46:39,100 --> 01:46:40,215
We can enter here...

1733
01:46:40,573 --> 01:46:42,400
as shown in these satellite photos.

1734
01:46:42,424 --> 01:46:43,800
We then upload the virus.

1735
01:46:43,825 --> 01:46:46,304
We then set off some kind of explosion,

1736
01:46:46,601 --> 01:46:47,875
which will disable it.

1737
01:46:47,900 --> 01:46:49,742
And that will disorient 
the smaller ships below.

1738
01:46:49,767 --> 01:46:52,310
And that could buy you
I think at least some time,

1739
01:46:52,334 --> 01:46:53,216
to...

1740
01:46:54,388 --> 01:46:55,552
to take them...

1741
01:46:55,797 --> 01:46:56,623
take them...

1742
01:46:56,755 --> 01:46:58,224
down, take them down.
Do your...

1743
01:46:59,565 --> 01:47:00,615
Do your stuff.

1744
01:47:00,950 --> 01:47:02,244
This is ridiculous!

1745
01:47:02,602 --> 01:47:04,357
How long would their shields be down?

1746
01:47:06,981 --> 01:47:08,400
I don't know. A matter of minutes.

1747
01:47:08,600 --> 01:47:11,000
You want us to coordinate
a massive worldwide counterstrike

1748
01:47:11,024 --> 01:47:13,600
with a window of only a few minutes?

1749
01:47:13,727 --> 01:47:15,587
With shields down
that might be possible.

1750
01:47:16,200 --> 01:47:17,174
Please!

1751
01:47:17,500 --> 01:47:19,588
We don't have the manpower or the resources

1752
01:47:19,612 --> 01:47:21,361
to launch that kind of a campaign!

1753
01:47:21,656 --> 01:47:23,875
Not to mention that this whole
cockamamie plan

1754
01:47:23,900 --> 01:47:27,700
is dependent on a machine that no one
in this world is qualified to operate.

1755
01:47:29,025 --> 01:47:30,400
I would not say that sir.

1756
01:47:30,775 --> 01:47:32,131
I have seen these things in action.

1757
01:47:32,156 --> 01:47:34,233
And I am well aware of their
maneuvering capabilities.

1758
01:47:36,179 --> 01:47:38,700
With your permission general
I would like the opportunity to try.

1759
01:47:39,600 --> 01:47:41,650
That thing is a wreck!

1760
01:47:42,733 --> 01:47:44,199
It crash-landed back in the '50s!

1761
01:47:44,200 --> 01:47:46,400
We don't even know if it's capable of flying!

1762
01:47:46,555 --> 01:47:47,342
Jim...

1763
01:47:48,115 --> 01:47:49,100
remove the clamps.

1764
01:48:11,550 --> 01:48:12,850
Any questions?

1765
01:48:17,950 --> 01:48:18,861
Let's do it.

1766
01:48:23,150 --> 01:48:25,105
Alright you heard the president
let's get this thing preped and ready to fly!

1767
01:48:25,130 --> 01:48:26,880
Good luck pilot.
Thank you Mr. President.

1768
01:48:28,662 --> 01:48:29,712
A virus!

1769
01:48:31,150 --> 01:48:32,200
Your idea.

1770
01:48:33,200 --> 01:48:34,196
That's right.

1771
01:48:40,950 --> 01:48:42,800
Do you really think you can fly that thing?

1772
01:48:44,100 --> 01:48:46,600
Do you really think you can do
all that bullshit you just said?

1773
01:48:56,200 --> 01:48:58,800
I understand, you are upset
over the death of your wife.

1774
01:48:58,825 --> 01:49:01,575
But that's no excuse for making
another fatal mistake.

1775
01:49:01,600 --> 01:49:03,776
No! The only mistake I ever made

1776
01:49:03,801 --> 01:49:06,841
was to appoint a sniveling little weasel
like you as Secretary of Defense.

1777
01:49:06,900 --> 01:49:08,645
I don't think you understand!
However!

1778
01:49:09,550 --> 01:49:11,798
That is one mistake I am thankful
to say that...

1779
01:49:12,016 --> 01:49:13,376
I don't have to live with.

1780
01:49:13,500 --> 01:49:15,100
Mr. President please!
Mr. Nimziki...

1781
01:49:16,000 --> 01:49:16,979
You are fired.

1782
01:49:20,718 --> 01:49:24,818
Let's organize every plane we can find
and get us some goddamn pilots to fly them.

1783
01:49:24,843 --> 01:49:25,877
Yes sir.

1784
01:49:26,550 --> 01:49:28,425
He can't do that.
Well he just...

1785
01:49:29,650 --> 01:49:30,650
did.

1786
01:49:34,359 --> 01:49:37,104
Command has attempted to compile
a list of casualties and losses

1787
01:49:37,129 --> 01:49:38,878
but information is sketchy at best.

1788
01:49:38,906 --> 01:49:41,401
Well we know we have lost
the Belgian contingent in the Sina.

1789
01:49:41,732 --> 01:49:45,782
There is a strong possibility there may be more
reinforcements hiding in the Golan Straits.

1790
01:49:49,200 --> 01:49:50,400
What the hell is he saying?

1791
01:49:50,425 --> 01:49:53,000
It seems they are getting a signal.
Old Morse code.

1792
01:50:05,998 --> 01:50:07,098
It's from the Americans!

1793
01:50:09,754 --> 01:50:11,691
They want to organize a counter offensive!

1794
01:50:11,869 --> 01:50:13,160
It's about bloody time!

1795
01:50:13,433 --> 01:50:14,824
What do they plan to do?

1796
01:50:37,250 --> 01:50:38,745
We have confirmed reports of...

1797
01:50:39,000 --> 01:50:41,247
combat ready divisions in Europe,

1798
01:50:41,271 --> 01:50:42,428
the Middle East and Asia.

1799
01:50:42,453 --> 01:50:43,578
That's impressive.

1800
01:50:43,771 --> 01:50:45,609
